  "section_notes": "S1 imposes safe reporting deadlines: 24h for serious incidents, 5 business days for other incidents, with reporting not delayed pending investigation. S2 sets a 5% failure limit and gives customers per-model results, but exceedance only triggers regulator review and corrective action rather than an automatic sales stop. S3 weakens new-unit shut-off to 24 months and retrofit to 6 years; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 mandates recall at 8/100k with immediate notices but no mandatory serious-injury recall clause."
